# The region painter is a build artifact rather than a script, so the pinned
# installer compiles it on first use. It is deliberately not resolved from a
# source checkout for the reason recorded above bonsai's resolver: a working
# tree is not the pinned closure, and a mask edited by a different build of
# the format is exactly the kind of divergence a pin exists to prevent.
# The camera viewer, resolved the same way and for the same reasons.  It is
# also in the content catalog, so `kilix install` and every desktop's menu
# reach the same pinned build this does - a camera watched from the Start
# menu and one watched from a pane must not be two different programs.
# The recorder, on the same shape as the viewer.  It is a separate verb
# rather than a mode of `rtsp` because they are different programs with
# different lifetimes: one shows you a camera now, the other runs for
# months and owns a database.
